des who who the hell is  this guy  i think he would be  quite befuddled i don't know that he  would actually be able to give me  much helpful advice about where i am or  what i should do or what activities i  should prioritize and which i should  downplay  and  this is not to say that we shouldn't try  to think about how we would relate  ourselves to our earlier  versions of our self  but  i don't think we should romanticize  youth i don't think we should say oh you  know  that person  was  more squared away that person  you know had the right values and maybe  i've lost my way i mean that could be  the case for for some of you who are  watching this  that sure as hell is not the case for me  and i suspect it's not the case for  many others so you know  um  again sort of a shoot if the shoe fit  wears it if this is actually helpful  advice for you and kind of shores up  your own willingness to say to people  who try to push this thing onto you no  no man i've i'm happy assessing myself  from my own vantage point or asking my  friends and colleagues and family  members in the present i don't need to  go back to  1985  or earlier or around that time to  bring up some memory of a person who is  probably  mostly made up  you know an earlier version of myself i  don't need to do that because i can  figure things out and  assess them  here in  the present  you

